+- **A pre-existing console error, found but not caused by this piece:** running the full `Recite.test.mjs` suite in a real browser (`mcp__servex__check_page`, not the pixel-only screenshot tool) shows `Recite: a listener failed TypeError: fn is not a function` a few times, from `Recite.changed()` during a `play()` call. `on()`, `set()` and `changed()` are untouched by echo or the thinking cue; `ReciteHighlight`'s own `recite.on(() => this.tick())` is the only subscriber and is always a valid function. The error is caught (`changed()`'s own try/catch) and every test still reports PASS — all 19 tests, 0 failed. Best guess: `TestBlocks.js` runs every `test()` in a file concurrently (each fires at module-eval time, not awaited one at a time) and shares one global `View.set_captor()` across them, plus the harness auto-draws whatever object a test `return`s in a live `DefaultView`; with 19 tests now in flight together (up from 15), the odds of two tests' construction/teardown interleaving badly went up enough to actually hit it. Not reproduced with a targeted, isolated run. Out of this piece's fence (core/Page's `DefaultView`/`core/Test`'s `TestBlocks.js`, not `audio/Recite`); logged here so it is not lost, not fixed here.
